    "turn_text": "Well, listen, I think it's fair. I think people are saying, well, he's just a sellout. I think if you're a Republican in this situation, you are just dealing with Trump above you. You're dealing with the base around you. He's the only African-American Republican that we have in the Congress. He's the only one who's been able to be as critical as he has been. If he's afraid to jump off of that diving board, I don't think people should attack him. I think we've got a much bigger problem, which is that the polarization in this country is such that no matter what anybody says about the other side, people are going to be dug into their tribal camps. I think there's plenty of evidence at this point that the president behaved in ways that are wrong. And also the brave Ukrainians who really that's the center of this thing you've got you cranium freedom fighters who are up against the biggest threat in the world who were relying on americans for help their plight got turned into a political football that is a tragedy and the fact that we can't even agree on that is i think a very very uh... bad sign",
